ABSTRACT_EN = [
    ("p", "This project studies joint dynamic channel assignment and routing in multi-hop Wi-Fi mesh networks. We propose EGAT-MAPPO, in which every node is an agent that chooses its downlink channel and its parent. The model combines an edge-aware graph attention encoder (GATv2), two decision timescales and a residual prior from Ko's local-cost rule. It is warm-started by behaviour cloning from Ko, trained with MAPPO, and executed in a decentralised way with switch hysteresis that suppresses unnecessary switches."),
    ("p", "We evaluate it in a custom Python simulator with an 802.11ax PHY and ns-3 default path loss: 20 nodes, two gateways and six downlink channels, across 11 scenarios. The baselines are a static assignment (M0), Ko, Q-neutral, Yuan (GAT+DQN) and Li (GAT-A2C). Every learned method is trained with five seeds and tested on 20 topologies per scenario. We use a pre-registered five-metric composite and intervals that count the training-seed variance of both methods."),
    ("p", "The simulator's airtime model is calibrated against packet-level ns-3 (7.4% rms error) before training. In the main setting, on a pre-registered set of fresh confirmation topologies (seeds 40-59), EGAT-MAPPO's composite exceeds every adapted published baseline by more than 10% (Ko +24.6%, Li +17.9%, Yuan +24.8%) and all four pre-registered criteria are met; the test topologies, a second fresh set and queue-preserving switches give the same picture. When Li and Yuan receive the same switch hysteresis, EGAT-MAPPO still beats both significantly (Li with hysteresis +10.7%, Yuan with hysteresis +6.7%). On the test topologies its throughput is 12.4% above Ko's with 93% fewer switches (42 versus 616 per episode). In ns-3 on three scenarios it significantly beats every method with and without RTS/CTS (Ko +23.1%, Yuan with hysteresis +16.4%). The final model drops the GRU memory after the ablation study, a change confirmed under a protocol fixed before the confirmation run on unused topologies."),
    ("p", "Keywords:  Channel assignment,  Routing,  Wi-Fi mesh,  Graph attention network,  MAPPO,  Multi-agent reinforcement learning"),
]

